{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent list"},{"type":"text","value":" discovers skill-enabled packages and shows the skills available under the project's permissions and exclusions. It does not change permissions or write guidance."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"list\",\"[--json]\",\"[--debug]\",\"[--global]\",\"[--global-only]\",\"[--show-hidden]\",\"[--no-notices]\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Output"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":": print structured skills, packages, and diagnostics instead of text output"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--debug"},{"type":"text","value":": print discovery details to stderr, including scan counts and package.json reads"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--show-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":": include a hidden-source summary in text output when run outside an agent session"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--no-notices"},{"type":"text","value":": suppress non-critical notices in text mode; the notice for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills: [\"*\"]"},{"type":"text","value":" remains visible"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"scan-scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scan scope"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--global"},{"type":"text","value":": include global packages after project packages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--global-only"},{"type":"text","value":": list global packages only"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"list"},{"type":"text","value":" is the consumer catalog for skills shipped by project and workspace dependencies. Library maintainers load Intent's packaged authoring procedures through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent meta"},{"type":"text","value":" or the installed maintainer block; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent maintainer"},{"type":"text","value":" handles setup, registration, synchronization, and checks."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"default-list","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default list"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intent scans project and workspace dependencies, applies "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json#intent.skills"},{"type":"text","value":", then removes packages and skills matched by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.exclude"},{"type":"text","value":". It uses project "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":" when available and Yarn's PnP API in PnP projects without usable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global packages are scanned only with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--global"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--global-only"},{"type":"text","value":". When both local and global copies of a package are found, the local copy takes precedence. Version conflicts show the chosen package and other discovered versions and paths."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"link","href":"./intent-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent install"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to configure permissions on first use. Listing skills does not open the install picker."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"which-skills-appear","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which skills appear"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The nearest configured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" list applies, including inherited workspace permissions. Each entry enables a package, a package pattern, or one exact skill:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Saved rule"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skills included"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Includes future additions?"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"*\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All discovered npm and workspace sources."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All packages and skills."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"@tanstack/query\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All skills in that npm package."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New skills in the package."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"@tanstack/*\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All skills in matching npm packages."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New matching packages and skills."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"@tanstack/query#fetching\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetching"},{"type":"text","value":" skill in that package."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only that skill name."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"workspace:@scope/internal\""}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All skills in that workspace package."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New skills in the package."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace patterns and individual skills also use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:"},{"type":"text","value":" prefix, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:@scope/*"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"workspace:@scope/internal#testing"},{"type":"text","value":". Package patterns support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":"; individual-skill entries require an exact package and skill name. Git sources are not supported."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No configured list:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" all discovered sources appear, with a migration notice. This is the existing-project upgrade path; a future version will require explicit permissions."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An empty list ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" no sources are permitted, with an informational notice."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All sources ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[\"*\"]"},{"type":"text","value":"):"}]},{"type":"text","value":" all discovered sources appear, with a notice that unvetted skills may enter agent guidance."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Permissions select sources and skill names. They do not freeze skill content when dependencies update. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/trust-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trust model"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"exclusions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exclusions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.exclude"},{"type":"text","value":" takes precedence over permissions. Intent combines exclusions from package.json files between the workspace or project root and the current directory."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exclusion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Effect"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/*devtools*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Excludes matching packages."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query#experimental-*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Excludes matching skills in that package."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*#experimental-*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Excludes matching skills across packages."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query#*"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Excludes the whole package."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only exact names and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":" wildcards are supported. Excluded packages do not trigger unlisted-source notices. Manage exclusions with "},{"type":"link","href":"./intent-exclude","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent exclude"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"hidden-sources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hidden sources"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Packages outside an explicit allowlist are omitted from the available catalog. In a human session, a policy notice names them; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--show-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":" adds their names and skill counts to the text output. This does not enable them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In agent sessions, hidden sources are reported by count only. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--show-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot reveal their identities there; run it outside the agent session to review candidates. A configured package or package pattern that was not discovered also produces a notice. So does an exact skill entry whose discovered package has no skill with that name."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text output includes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A summary with package and skill counts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A package table with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PACKAGE"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SOURCE"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VERSION"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILLS"},{"type":"text","value":" columns."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A skill tree grouped by package, with descriptions and commands to load each skill."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version conflicts and discovery warnings, when present."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Load commands use the detected package manager's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/intent@latest"},{"type":"text","value":" runner and preserve the selected global scan scope. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SOURCE"},{"type":"text","value":" distinguishes local discovery from explicit global scanning."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text output and discovery warnings go to stdout. Policy notices and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--debug"},{"type":"text","value":" details go to stderr."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"json-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":" prints a structured catalog to stdout. This example shows one available skill with no hidden sources or diagnostics; paths and package metadata vary by project:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"skills\": [\n    {\n      \"use\": \"@tanstack/query#fetching\",\n      \"packageName\": \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"packageRoot\": \"/path/to/project/node_modules/@tanstack/query\",\n      \"packageVersion\": \"5.0.0\",\n      \"packageSource\": \"local\",\n      \"skillName\": \"fetching\",\n      \"description\": \"Use when fetching and caching server data with TanStack Query.\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Query data fetching patterns\",\n      \"type\": \"core\",\n      \"framework\": \"react\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"packages\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"version\": \"5.0.0\",\n      \"source\": \"local\",\n      \"packageRoot\": \"/path/to/project/node_modules/@tanstack/query\",\n      \"skillCount\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hiddenSourceCount\": 0,\n  \"hiddenSources\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"notices\": [],\n  \"conflicts\": []\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available skills. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"use"},{"type":"text","value":" is the portable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<package>#<skill>"},{"type":"text","value":" identity; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"framework"},{"type":"text","value":" are optional."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard agent-discovery text describing when to use the skill. Also used in the text listing."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"purpose"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional descriptive explanation from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata.purpose"},{"type":"text","value":", kept separate from activation guidance. Omitted from JSON when absent."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Selected packages, their source and location, and permitted skill counts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hiddenSourceCount"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Number of packages hidden by the explicit allowlist."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hiddenSources"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Objects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skillCount"},{"type":"text","value":" in human sessions, even without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--show-hidden"},{"type":"text","value":". Always empty in agent sessions."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"warnings"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery warnings."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notices"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy and migration notices. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--no-notices"},{"type":"text","value":" does not remove these from JSON."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conflicts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Objects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packageName"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chosen"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"variants"},{"type":"text","value":". Each chosen or variant entry contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"version"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packageRoot"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON includes diagnostics in the object instead of printing separate warning or notice blocks. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--debug"},{"type":"text","value":" still writes to stderr. Treat identifiers as data when constructing commands; JSON does not contain shell-escaped arguments."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"status-messages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status messages"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Message or behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No selected packages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"No intent-enabled packages found."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available catalog"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<package count> intent-enabled packages, <skill count> skills"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by the table and tree."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version conflicts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Version conflicts:"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by the chosen version and other discovered locations."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hidden-source review"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hidden skill sources:"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by names and skill counts in a human session."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hidden-source review in an agent session"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hidden skill sources are not revealed in agent sessions. Run this command outside the agent session to review candidates."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery warnings"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Warnings:"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"⚠"},{"type":"text","value":" messages on stdout in text mode."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy notices"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Notices:"},{"type":"text","value":" followed by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ℹ"},{"type":"text","value":" messages on stderr in text mode."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common errors"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalid permissions or unreadable policy files:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Intent stops and reports the problem. Fix the reported package.json or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" entry before retrying."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unsupported runnable identifier:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" generated commands accept only ASCII letters, numbers, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"."},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-"},{"type":"text","value":". Identifiers cannot start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#"},{"type":"text","value":"; leading and trailing whitespace is rejected rather than trimmed. Rename the package or skill to generate runnable guidance. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":" can still expose permitted identifiers as data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unreadable or out-of-package skill metadata:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" discovery skips skill files whose real path cannot be resolved or lies outside the package root, with a warning. It checks the opened file's identity before reading and uses that descriptor for the full metadata read, including large frontmatter, so later pathname replacement cannot redirect the read. Symlinks within the resolved package root remain supported."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deno without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"text","value":" this discovery mode is unsupported."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent install"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-load","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent load"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent meta"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-exclude","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent exclude"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../concepts/trust-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trust model"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"output","text":"Output","level":3},{"id":"scan-scope","text":"Scan scope","level":3},{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"default-list","text":"Default list","level":3},{"id":"which-skills-appear","text":"Which skills appear","level":3},{"id":"exclusions","text":"Exclusions","level":3},{"id":"hidden-sources","text":"Hidden sources","level":3},{"id":"default-output","text":"Default output","level":2},{"id":"json-output","text":"JSON output","level":2},{"id":"status-messages","text":"Status messages","level":2},{"id":"common-errors","text":"Common errors","level":2},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`intent list` discovers skill-enabled packages and shows the skills available under the project's permissions and exclusions. It does not change permissions or write guidance.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list [--json] [--debug] [--global] [--global-only] [--show-hidden] [--no-notices]\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Options\n\n### Output\n\n- `--json`: print structured skills, packages, and diagnostics instead of text output\n- `--debug`: print discovery details to stderr, including scan counts and package.json reads\n- `--show-hidden`: include a hidden-source summary in text output when run outside an agent session\n- `--no-notices`: suppress non-critical notices in text mode; the notice for `intent.skills: [\"*\"]` remains visible\n\n### Scan scope\n\n- `--global`: include global packages after project packages\n- `--global-only`: list global packages only\n\n## Behavior\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `list` is the consumer catalog for skills shipped by project and workspace dependencies. Library maintainers load Intent's packaged authoring procedures through `intent meta` or the installed maintainer block; `intent maintainer` handles setup, registration, synchronization, and checks.\n\n### Default list\n\nIntent scans project and workspace dependencies, applies `package.json#intent.skills`, then removes packages and skills matched by `intent.exclude`. It uses project `node_modules` when available and Yarn's PnP API in PnP projects without usable `node_modules`.\n\nGlobal packages are scanned only with `--global` or `--global-only`. When both local and global copies of a package are found, the local copy takes precedence. Version conflicts show the chosen package and other discovered versions and paths.\n\nRun [intent install](./intent-install) to configure permissions on first use. Listing skills does not open the install picker.\n\n### Which skills appear\n\nThe nearest configured `intent.skills` list applies, including inherited workspace permissions. Each entry enables a package, a package pattern, or one exact skill:\n\n| Saved rule | Skills included | Includes future additions? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `\"*\"` | All discovered npm and workspace sources. | All packages and skills. |\n| `\"@tanstack/query\"` | All skills in that npm package. | New skills in the package. |\n| `\"@tanstack/*\"` | All skills in matching npm packages. | New matching packages and skills. |\n| `\"@tanstack/query#fetching\"` | The `fetching` skill in that package. | Only that skill name. |\n| `\"workspace:@scope/internal\"` | All skills in that workspace package. | New skills in the package. |\n\nWorkspace patterns and individual skills also use the `workspace:` prefix, such as `workspace:@scope/*` and `workspace:@scope/internal#testing`. Package patterns support `*`; individual-skill entries require an exact package and skill name. Git sources are not supported.\n\n- **No configured list:** all discovered sources appear, with a migration notice. This is the existing-project upgrade path; a future version will require explicit permissions.\n- **An empty list (`[]`):** no sources are permitted, with an informational notice.\n- **All sources (`[\"*\"]`):** all discovered sources appear, with a notice that unvetted skills may enter agent guidance.\n\nPermissions select sources and skill names. They do not freeze skill content when dependencies update. See [Configuration](../concepts/configuration) and [Trust model](../concepts/trust-model).\n\n### Exclusions\n\n`intent.exclude` takes precedence over permissions. Intent combines exclusions from package.json files between the workspace or project root and the current directory.\n\n| Exclusion | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `@tanstack/*devtools*` | Excludes matching packages. |\n| `@tanstack/query#experimental-*` | Excludes matching skills in that package. |\n| `*#experimental-*` | Excludes matching skills across packages. |\n| `@tanstack/query#*` | Excludes the whole package. |\n\nOnly exact names and `*` wildcards are supported. Excluded packages do not trigger unlisted-source notices. Manage exclusions with [intent exclude](./intent-exclude).\n\n### Hidden sources\n\nPackages outside an explicit allowlist are omitted from the available catalog. In a human session, a policy notice names them; `--show-hidden` adds their names and skill counts to the text output. This does not enable them.\n\nIn agent sessions, hidden sources are reported by count only. `--show-hidden` cannot reveal their identities there; run it outside the agent session to review candidates. A configured package or package pattern that was not discovered also produces a notice. So does an exact skill entry whose discovered package has no skill with that name.\n\n## Default output\n\nText output includes:\n\n- A summary with package and skill counts.\n- A package table with `PACKAGE`, `SOURCE`, `VERSION`, and `SKILLS` columns.\n- A skill tree grouped by package, with descriptions and commands to load each skill.\n- Version conflicts and discovery warnings, when present.\n\nLoad commands use the detected package manager's `@tanstack/intent@latest` runner and preserve the selected global scan scope. `SOURCE` distinguishes local discovery from explicit global scanning.\n\nText output and discovery warnings go to stdout. Policy notices and `--debug` details go to stderr.\n\n## JSON output\n\n`--json` prints a structured catalog to stdout. This example shows one available skill with no hidden sources or diagnostics; paths and package metadata vary by project:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skills\": [\n    {\n      \"use\": \"@tanstack/query#fetching\",\n      \"packageName\": \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"packageRoot\": \"/path/to/project/node_modules/@tanstack/query\",\n      \"packageVersion\": \"5.0.0\",\n      \"packageSource\": \"local\",\n      \"skillName\": \"fetching\",\n      \"description\": \"Use when fetching and caching server data with TanStack Query.\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Query data fetching patterns\",\n      \"type\": \"core\",\n      \"framework\": \"react\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"packages\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"version\": \"5.0.0\",\n      \"source\": \"local\",\n      \"packageRoot\": \"/path/to/project/node_modules/@tanstack/query\",\n      \"skillCount\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hiddenSourceCount\": 0,\n  \"hiddenSources\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"notices\": [],\n  \"conflicts\": []\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `skills` | Available skills. `use` is the portable `<package>#<skill>` identity; `type` and `framework` are optional. |\n| Skill `description` | Standard agent-discovery text describing when to use the skill. Also used in the text listing. |\n| Skill `purpose` | Optional descriptive explanation from `metadata.purpose`, kept separate from activation guidance. Omitted from JSON when absent. |\n| `packages` | Selected packages, their source and location, and permitted skill counts. |\n| `hiddenSourceCount` | Number of packages hidden by the explicit allowlist. |\n| `hiddenSources` | Objects with `name` and `skillCount` in human sessions, even without `--show-hidden`. Always empty in agent sessions. |\n| `warnings` | Discovery warnings. |\n| `notices` | Policy and migration notices. `--no-notices` does not remove these from JSON. |\n| `conflicts` | Objects with `packageName`, `chosen`, and `variants`. Each chosen or variant entry contains `version` and `packageRoot`. |\n\nJSON includes diagnostics in the object instead of printing separate warning or notice blocks. `--debug` still writes to stderr. Treat identifiers as data when constructing commands; JSON does not contain shell-escaped arguments.\n\n## Status messages\n\n| Result | Message or behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| No selected packages | `No intent-enabled packages found.` |\n| Available catalog | `<package count> intent-enabled packages, <skill count> skills` followed by the table and tree. |\n| Version conflicts | `Version conflicts:` followed by the chosen version and other discovered locations. |\n| Hidden-source review | `Hidden skill sources:` followed by names and skill counts in a human session. |\n| Hidden-source review in an agent session | `Hidden skill sources are not revealed in agent sessions. Run this command outside the agent session to review candidates.` |\n| Discovery warnings | `Warnings:` followed by `⚠` messages on stdout in text mode. |\n| Policy notices | `Notices:` followed by `ℹ` messages on stderr in text mode. |\n\n## Common errors\n\n- **Invalid permissions or unreadable policy files:** Intent stops and reports the problem. Fix the reported package.json or `intent.skills` entry before retrying.\n- **Unsupported runnable identifier:** generated commands accept only ASCII letters, numbers, `_`, `.`, `/`, `@`, `#`, and `-`. Identifiers cannot start with `#`; leading and trailing whitespace is rejected rather than trimmed. Rename the package or skill to generate runnable guidance. `--json` can still expose permitted identifiers as data.\n- **Unreadable or out-of-package skill metadata:** discovery skips skill files whose real path cannot be resolved or lies outside the package root, with a warning. It checks the opened file's identity before reading and uses that descriptor for the full metadata read, including large frontmatter, so later pathname replacement cannot redirect the read. Symlinks within the resolved package root remain supported.\n- **Deno without `node_modules`:** this discovery mode is unsupported.\n\n## Related\n\n- [intent install](./intent-install)\n- [intent load](./intent-load)\n- [intent meta](./intent-meta)\n- [intent exclude](./intent-exclude)\n- [Configuration](../concepts/configuration)\n- [Trust model](../concepts/trust-model)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: intent list\nid: intent-list\n---\n\n`intent list` discovers skill-enabled packages and shows the skills available under the project's permissions and exclusions. It does not change permissions or write guidance.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest list [--json] [--debug] [--global] [--global-only] [--show-hidden] [--no-notices]\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Options\n\n### Output\n\n- `--json`: print structured skills, packages, and diagnostics instead of text output\n- `--debug`: print discovery details to stderr, including scan counts and package.json reads\n- `--show-hidden`: include a hidden-source summary in text output when run outside an agent session\n- `--no-notices`: suppress non-critical notices in text mode; the notice for `intent.skills: [\"*\"]` remains visible\n\n### Scan scope\n\n- `--global`: include global packages after project packages\n- `--global-only`: list global packages only\n\n## Behavior\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> `list` is the consumer catalog for skills shipped by project and workspace dependencies. Library maintainers load Intent's packaged authoring procedures through `intent meta` or the installed maintainer block; `intent maintainer` handles setup, registration, synchronization, and checks.\n\n### Default list\n\nIntent scans project and workspace dependencies, applies `package.json#intent.skills`, then removes packages and skills matched by `intent.exclude`. It uses project `node_modules` when available and Yarn's PnP API in PnP projects without usable `node_modules`.\n\nGlobal packages are scanned only with `--global` or `--global-only`. When both local and global copies of a package are found, the local copy takes precedence. Version conflicts show the chosen package and other discovered versions and paths.\n\nRun [intent install](./intent-install) to configure permissions on first use. Listing skills does not open the install picker.\n\n### Which skills appear\n\nThe nearest configured `intent.skills` list applies, including inherited workspace permissions. Each entry enables a package, a package pattern, or one exact skill:\n\n| Saved rule | Skills included | Includes future additions? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `\"*\"` | All discovered npm and workspace sources. | All packages and skills. |\n| `\"@tanstack/query\"` | All skills in that npm package. | New skills in the package. |\n| `\"@tanstack/*\"` | All skills in matching npm packages. | New matching packages and skills. |\n| `\"@tanstack/query#fetching\"` | The `fetching` skill in that package. | Only that skill name. |\n| `\"workspace:@scope/internal\"` | All skills in that workspace package. | New skills in the package. |\n\nWorkspace patterns and individual skills also use the `workspace:` prefix, such as `workspace:@scope/*` and `workspace:@scope/internal#testing`. Package patterns support `*`; individual-skill entries require an exact package and skill name. Git sources are not supported.\n\n- **No configured list:** all discovered sources appear, with a migration notice. This is the existing-project upgrade path; a future version will require explicit permissions.\n- **An empty list (`[]`):** no sources are permitted, with an informational notice.\n- **All sources (`[\"*\"]`):** all discovered sources appear, with a notice that unvetted skills may enter agent guidance.\n\nPermissions select sources and skill names. They do not freeze skill content when dependencies update. See [Configuration](../concepts/configuration) and [Trust model](../concepts/trust-model).\n\n### Exclusions\n\n`intent.exclude` takes precedence over permissions. Intent combines exclusions from package.json files between the workspace or project root and the current directory.\n\n| Exclusion | Effect |\n| --- | --- |\n| `@tanstack/*devtools*` | Excludes matching packages. |\n| `@tanstack/query#experimental-*` | Excludes matching skills in that package. |\n| `*#experimental-*` | Excludes matching skills across packages. |\n| `@tanstack/query#*` | Excludes the whole package. |\n\nOnly exact names and `*` wildcards are supported. Excluded packages do not trigger unlisted-source notices. Manage exclusions with [intent exclude](./intent-exclude).\n\n### Hidden sources\n\nPackages outside an explicit allowlist are omitted from the available catalog. In a human session, a policy notice names them; `--show-hidden` adds their names and skill counts to the text output. This does not enable them.\n\nIn agent sessions, hidden sources are reported by count only. `--show-hidden` cannot reveal their identities there; run it outside the agent session to review candidates. A configured package or package pattern that was not discovered also produces a notice. So does an exact skill entry whose discovered package has no skill with that name.\n\n## Default output\n\nText output includes:\n\n- A summary with package and skill counts.\n- A package table with `PACKAGE`, `SOURCE`, `VERSION`, and `SKILLS` columns.\n- A skill tree grouped by package, with descriptions and commands to load each skill.\n- Version conflicts and discovery warnings, when present.\n\nLoad commands use the detected package manager's `@tanstack/intent@latest` runner and preserve the selected global scan scope. `SOURCE` distinguishes local discovery from explicit global scanning.\n\nText output and discovery warnings go to stdout. Policy notices and `--debug` details go to stderr.\n\n## JSON output\n\n`--json` prints a structured catalog to stdout. This example shows one available skill with no hidden sources or diagnostics; paths and package metadata vary by project:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skills\": [\n    {\n      \"use\": \"@tanstack/query#fetching\",\n      \"packageName\": \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"packageRoot\": \"/path/to/project/node_modules/@tanstack/query\",\n      \"packageVersion\": \"5.0.0\",\n      \"packageSource\": \"local\",\n      \"skillName\": \"fetching\",\n      \"description\": \"Use when fetching and caching server data with TanStack Query.\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Query data fetching patterns\",\n      \"type\": \"core\",\n      \"framework\": \"react\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"packages\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"@tanstack/query\",\n      \"version\": \"5.0.0\",\n      \"source\": \"local\",\n      \"packageRoot\": \"/path/to/project/node_modules/@tanstack/query\",\n      \"skillCount\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hiddenSourceCount\": 0,\n  \"hiddenSources\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"notices\": [],\n  \"conflicts\": []\n}\n```\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `skills` | Available skills. `use` is the portable `<package>#<skill>` identity; `type` and `framework` are optional. |\n| Skill `description` | Standard agent-discovery text describing when to use the skill. Also used in the text listing. |\n| Skill `purpose` | Optional descriptive explanation from `metadata.purpose`, kept separate from activation guidance. Omitted from JSON when absent. |\n| `packages` | Selected packages, their source and location, and permitted skill counts. |\n| `hiddenSourceCount` | Number of packages hidden by the explicit allowlist. |\n| `hiddenSources` | Objects with `name` and `skillCount` in human sessions, even without `--show-hidden`. Always empty in agent sessions. |\n| `warnings` | Discovery warnings. |\n| `notices` | Policy and migration notices. `--no-notices` does not remove these from JSON. |\n| `conflicts` | Objects with `packageName`, `chosen`, and `variants`. Each chosen or variant entry contains `version` and `packageRoot`. |\n\nJSON includes diagnostics in the object instead of printing separate warning or notice blocks. `--debug` still writes to stderr. Treat identifiers as data when constructing commands; JSON does not contain shell-escaped arguments.\n\n## Status messages\n\n| Result | Message or behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| No selected packages | `No intent-enabled packages found.` |\n| Available catalog | `<package count> intent-enabled packages, <skill count> skills` followed by the table and tree. |\n| Version conflicts | `Version conflicts:` followed by the chosen version and other discovered locations. |\n| Hidden-source review | `Hidden skill sources:` followed by names and skill counts in a human session. |\n| Hidden-source review in an agent session | `Hidden skill sources are not revealed in agent sessions. Run this command outside the agent session to review candidates.` |\n| Discovery warnings | `Warnings:` followed by `⚠` messages on stdout in text mode. |\n| Policy notices | `Notices:` followed by `ℹ` messages on stderr in text mode. |\n\n## Common errors\n\n- **Invalid permissions or unreadable policy files:** Intent stops and reports the problem. Fix the reported package.json or `intent.skills` entry before retrying.\n- **Unsupported runnable identifier:** generated commands accept only ASCII letters, numbers, `_`, `.`, `/`, `@`, `#`, and `-`. Identifiers cannot start with `#`; leading and trailing whitespace is rejected rather than trimmed. Rename the package or skill to generate runnable guidance. `--json` can still expose permitted identifiers as data.\n- **Unreadable or out-of-package skill metadata:** discovery skips skill files whose real path cannot be resolved or lies outside the package root, with a warning. It checks the opened file's identity before reading and uses that descriptor for the full metadata read, including large frontmatter, so later pathname replacement cannot redirect the read. Symlinks within the resolved package root remain supported.\n- **Deno without `node_modules`:** this discovery mode is unsupported.\n\n## Related\n\n- [intent install](./intent-install)\n- [intent load](./intent-load)\n- [intent meta](./intent-meta)\n- [intent exclude](./intent-exclude)\n- [Configuration](../concepts/configuration)\n- [Trust model](../concepts/trust-model)\n"}
